# SOURCE=physical GameCube
# GBP_PRESENT=yes
# PHYSICAL_RUN_ID=GBP-VIDEO-002
# TEST_ID=GBP-VIDEO-002
# BUILD_ID=vstate-0001
# DOL=vstate-0001
# COMMIT=e8f3a69
# COMMIT_FULL=e8f3a69e3ba190daf5db6954015a6fdae9aef6d7
# DOL_SHA256=c73d49fa39ff0878324cda20abb6da5058092cbc89c87d6fd3e6cd2abdac19b9
# LOG_SHA256=4f30d1cd8e315158a0b2ef3287256fa9a72d3a21e0977a9d42fe21699d576cfc
# LOG_SIZE=81380
# BLOCKS=hw-gamecube-gbp-2026-09-16-vstate-0001-vstate.bin
# BLOCKS_SHA256=6406f2444331ed099d141022e9d10d4c16ba120e0b13c6005e0a933756712639
# BLOCKS_SIZE=2432396
# BLOCKS_FORMAT=OGBPSEQ1 v2 (frame signatures + events + episode descriptors + sampled cycles + preserved raw)
# CAPTURED=2026-09-16
# NOTE=GBP-VIDEO-002 PHYSICALLY EXECUTED 2026-09-16, one run, no Game Pak. 51751 admitted cycles of the repeated drained service over 8.187 s. SERVICE FAILED at cycle 51750 with READ_semantic_disagree; every other dimension is independent and valid: FRAME_CAPTURE ok, BASELINE valid, STRUCTURED_CHANGE observed, RESTORE ok. 51750 ACK and 51750 re-arms completed, 51751 ISR entries, 0 reentry, 0 main W1C, 0 teardown W1C, 0 timeouts, 0 busy, 0 uncertain writes, 0 counter overflows.
# NOTE=THIS SCRIPT IS A PREFIX, NOT THE RUN. It carries the 003A stage, the FOUR verify cycles and the teardown - the only parts of this experiment whose transport operations the log records. The other 51746 cycles are LEAN by design (GBP-VIDEO-002 keeps no per-delivery record: ~639000 deliveries were expected), so their operations were never written and are NOT invented here. The evidence for those cycles is the per-frame signature store in the sidecar, not an operation stream.
# NOTE=the sidecar is the primary evidence: 489 frame records of 40 semantic signatures each, 209 events, 4 episode descriptors, 81 sampled cycle records and 15 preserved raw frames (15 x 40 x 0xF00 = 2304000 bytes), plus the first and last AUDIO drains. Header CRC 947083c4, total CRC 9bef714b, both recomputed on parse. Every one of the 600 preserved raw blocks reproduces its stored signature exactly.
# NOTE=THE OFFENDING RAW BLOCK OF THE ABORT IS NOT PRESERVED. At cycle 51750 the ISR fired normally (latency 34 ticks, INTSR bit 13 set at entry and cleared by its single W1C), the 32-byte IRQ read returned rc=ok, and the two semantic interpretations of that block disagreed: the Start-up Disc reading (bytes 0x1D and 0x1F) against GBI's reading (a majority vote over the eight replicas at offsets 1 and 3 of each group). The probe treats that as fatal and stopped before any ACK or re-arm. The 32 bytes, the two conflicting values and the pending source were NOT recorded: the cycle record carries pend=0000 and no payload. They are unrecoverable from this run and are NOT reconstructed here.
# NOTE=frame segmentation: 490 Disc boundaries, 490 GBI boundaries, ZERO predicate disagreements over 19513 VIDEO blocks. 489 intervals observed: 477 of exactly 40 blocks, plus 1x30, 4x34 and 7x38. Median boundary-to-boundary period 678084 ticks = 16.7428 ms = 59.727 Hz over 465 consecutive complete pairs.
# NOTE=the run settled into ONE signature vector repeated for 274 consecutive frames (215..488, 4.582 s) whose blocks 12..19 differ from the uniform white frame. That vector matches GBI reference table B in ALL FORTY blocks; it matches neither table A (26/40) nor the Start-up Disc's embedded frame (25/40). The reference data is read from the private inputs at analysis time and is never stored in this repository.
# NOTE=reconstructing the preserved raw frames as both references read them - pixel = byte1:byte3, bit 15 the frame marker, 4 lines per block, 240 pixels per line, 40 blocks - produces a legible animated GAME BOY logotype at 240x160. The colour channel order is NOT settled by this run and stays as EVIDENCE.md classifies it.
# NOTE=the EIGHT "B" lines are the four verify cycles' whole-block reads (4 AUDIO 0x1000 at 0x01800000, 4 VIDEO 0xF00 at 0x01100000). NONE of them is payload-backed: the v2 sidecar preserves raw by FRAME (15 complete 40-block frames belonging to episodes) and two AUDIO drains, not by cycle, so there is no mapping from a verify cycle's read to stored bytes. A replay reports them as missing blocks rather than inventing any, and no CRC is claimed for them.
# NOTE=INTSR polling loops replay with one time-base read per sample, so poll counters differ from the device run; every other value is the console's.
# generated by tools/probelog.py from a device log
